How I would upgrade RHEL version from one to another
-----------------------------------------------------
I would use the Leapp utility, which is Red Hat’s supported in-place upgrade framework for major version upgrades
from RHEL 9 to RHEL 10

1. First, I verify prerequisites
=================================
Before starting the upgrade, I check:
                                Current OS version
                                Active Red Hat subscription
                                Repository availability
                                Hardware and application compatibility
                                Third-party packages and kernel modules
                      Example commands:
                                        cat /etc/redhat-release
                                        subscription-manager status
                                        dnf repolist
                                        uname -r
I also verify whether applications support RHEL 10 because some drivers or packages may not be compatible after upgrade.

2. Take backup and rollback plan
=================================
Before any major upgrade, I ensure rollback capability.
For VMs:  Take VMware/Hyper-V snapshot
For physical servers: Take filesystem backup using rsync/tar or enterprise backup tools
